# Environment configuration for the Trading Intelligence System.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env.
#
# This file intentionally does NOT list any AI, market data, news, or
# broker/exchange provider keys yet — no provider has been chosen or
# confirmed. Sections for those will be added here once each agent's
# actual data source/provider is specified; nothing is assumed or
# invented ahead of that.
#
# Three environments are recognized (see README.md's Environments
# section for detail):
#   development — local iteration, synthetic/caller-supplied data only
#   test        — `npm test`; synthetic in-memory fixtures only, must
#                 never require real credentials
#   production   — FUTURE; real provider adapters, real credentials
#                 (once built — see README.md's Provider Integration Plan)
# No real credentials exist in this repo in any environment today.

# Port the (future) service listens on. Optional.
PORT=3000

# Environment name: development | test | production.
NODE_ENV=development

# --- Provider credentials (FUTURE — none exist yet) -----------------
# Once a specific market data / news / macro / sentiment provider is
# chosen (see README.md's Provider Integration Plan), that provider's
# adapter will read its own credential(s) here, e.g.:
#   MARKET_DATA_API_KEY=
#   NEWS_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
#   MACRO_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
#   SENTIMENT_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
# None of these are defined yet — no provider has been selected, and
# no code reads any of them. Do not add real values until a real
# adapter that consumes them exists.
